<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  REV Finance - Phase 4 security role, shipped as a solution component (WBS 8.2, automation
  #8, Finance: Provider, Bank Account & Payment).

  Held by Revitalise's finance role - a single 0.5 FTE post (docs/plans/revitalise-payment-
  capture-plan.md line 30). The only human-held role that ever sees bank details (NFR-002);
  REV Admin deliberately holds zero table privilege on rev_bankaccount/rev_payment (see that
  role's own header) and REV_FinanceOnly's column security is the second, independent layer
  of the same control. This role has no Applicant or Application privilege at all - the
  finance persona records payments, it never sees case data (US-015 AC-2).

  BUILD SPECIFICATION: docs/architecture/revitalise-grant-automation-architecture.md
  section 6.2 (the four-role table) and section 6.2.1 ("The Finance role does not exist -
  what wbs:8.3 assumes, and what wbs:8.2 must deliver"), which is this file's authoritative
  source. Two of the privilege grants below are CORRECTIONS the reviewer confirmed on
  2026-09-09 against section 6.2's originally-approved row, not the row as first written:
  Provider is Create/Read/Update (was "read" only), and this role additionally holds
  Read + AppendTo on rev_grant and Append on rev_payment (the approved row named no Grant
  privilege at all, which cannot be right - a Payment cannot reference a Grant this role
  cannot read, per FR-151). See section 6.2.1's own numbered deliverable table for the full
  reasoning behind both corrections.

  ONE STATED CONSEQUENCE OF THE rev_grant READ GRANT, RECORDED RATHER THAN SILENTLY ACCEPTED
  (docs/architecture/revitalise-grant-automation-architecture.md section 6.2.1, measured
  2026-09-09): rev_grant.rev_amountawarded is IsSecured=1, but Dataverse maintains
  rev_amountawarded_base alongside it with CanBeSecuredForRead=False, so column security does
  not withhold the awarded amount from any role holding table Read on rev_grant - the TABLE
  PRIVILEGE is the only control here. This role is judged entitled to that figure (it exists
  to pay the awarded amount, and FR-151 requires a Payment to reference its Grant), so this is
  an accepted, stated consequence of the grant above, not an oversight.

  OUT OF THIS FILE'S SCOPE, NAMED RATHER THAN SILENTLY OMITTED: section 6.2's summary row also
  lists "Signed-PDF library: read" for this persona. That is a SharePoint Online permission
  (ADR-014 - signed PDFs live in a SharePoint library linked by URL, not Dataverse document
  management), not a Dataverse security-role privilege, so there is nothing to add to this
  file for it. It is not built by wbs:8.2 and is not listed in section 6.2.1's own numbered
  deliverable table (7 items, all reproduced below) - flagged for whoever next touches
  SharePoint library permissions, not assumed solved here.

  ALSO OUT OF SCOPE: rev_roundfinance. REV Admin's own header records that it is the INTERIM
  maintainer of that table "until the REV Finance role exists in solution source" (WBS 6.9,
  A-R25) - now that this file exists, whether that interim arrangement should transfer is a
  question for whoever owns WBS 6.9/8.x's finance-figures automation, not this dispatch:
  section 6.2.1's deliverable table for THIS task does not mention rev_roundfinance at all,
  and adding an unrequested table privilege here would be scope creep on wbs:8.2, not a
  correction. REV Admin's existing rev_roundfinance privileges are left untouched.

  HOW THIS ROLE IS ASSIGNED
  Never directly to a user in TST/ACC or PRD. The only approved mechanism is
  Entra security group -> Dataverse group team (type AAD Security Group) -> this role,
  applied by provisioning/dataverse/bind-roles-to-groups.ps1 which looks the role up BY NAME
  because role GUIDs differ per environment (C-TECH-040, TAD section 6.1, ADR-008).
  Direct assignment is permitted in DEV only. Per TAD section 6.2.1 deliverable #6, the group
  team is "REV Finance", backed by Entra security group
  REV-PP-GrantApplications-Finance-<ACC|PRD> - see provisioning/deploymentSettings/
  test-settings.json and prd-settings.json, both edited alongside this file.

  THIS IS A NEW CUSTOM ROLE, NOT A MODIFIED OUT-OF-BOX ROLE (C-TECH-046).
  TAD section 6.2 records the deliberate decision NOT to use a shared "[PREFIX] Base User"
  base-plus-additive role, because this role must have no access to Applicant, Application,
  Review or Setting - a shared base would either over-grant or be empty. Each persona role is
  therefore self-sufficient, which is why the platform baseline block below is the same block
  REV Admin and REV Trustee both carry.

  WARNING FOR THE REVIEWER - the platform baseline block's PRIVILEGE NAMES are already
  confirmed to exist in this Dataverse environment: they are the exact post-correction set
  validated live on 2026-08-14 (REV Admin, REV Service Automation) and reused unchanged for
  REV Trustee on 2026-08-21 (prvReadSavedQuery and prvReadEnvironmentVariableValue removed,
  both confirmed absent from this environment - see those files' own headers). Copying that
  confirmed set here is lower risk than the original guess was. What is still UNVERIFIED for
  this role specifically: (1) the role has never itself been created in DEV, so the
  create-role event (step 5 of ensure-schema.ps1) is unproven for a fourth role even though
  the privilege names it will request are all already known good; (2) whether the full
  MDA-oriented baseline (personal views, web resources) is necessary for a persona whose only
  screen is the payment-capture area of the existing REV Grant Administration model-driven
  app (wbs:8.3, ADR-048) is assumed by analogy with the other MDA personas, not tested against
  a live finance user yet.

    A-FIN-09 | Claim: the platform baseline block (prvReadUserQuery/Create/Write/Delete
    "Basic", prvReadWebResource "Global", and the rest of the block copied from REV Admin/
    REV Trustee) is necessary and sufficient for this persona, not merely harmless | Where:
    RolePrivileges block below, the "Platform baseline" section | Evidence: E3 - by analogy
    with the two MDA-persona sibling roles; no live finance user exists yet to test the
    narrower alternative against | Why not verified: the role has never been created in DEV
    and wbs:8.3's payment-capture form/app-sharing has not reached V4 | Cheapest
    verification: after wbs:8.2's live role-create (REVIEWER ACTION REQUIRED block below) and
    wbs:8.3's app-sharing land, sign in as a test finance user, open REV Grant Administration,
    confirm the payment-capture area opens and every Bank Account/Payment field is populated
    (not blank - see the V4 blocker section 6.2.1 names), then decide whether to narrow the
    baseline | Status: OPEN

  COLUMN-LEVEL SECURITY IS NOT IN THIS FILE. Table privileges below make rows visible; they do
  not release a single one of the 16 IsSecured=1 columns on rev_bankaccount/rev_payment. That
  release is REV_FinanceOnly (Other/FieldSecurityProfiles.xml), whose MEMBERSHIP is applied
  per environment by provisioning/dataverse/ensure-column-security-profile-members.ps1 and,
  per this dispatch, by adding "REV Finance" to that profile's memberTeams array in
  provisioning/deploymentSettings/test-settings.json and prd-settings.json (TAD section 6.2.1
  deliverable #5) - not by editing FieldSecurityProfiles.xml itself, which already ships the
  profile and its 16 column entries unchanged (built under WBS 0.4's remainder).

  THE id BELOW IS DEV'S REAL, LIVE roleid, NOT A FABRICATED ONE.

    A-FIN-10 | CLOSED 2026-09-13. Claim: "REV Finance" did not exist in any environment |
    Where: this Role element's id attribute, and the matching
    <RootComponent type="20"> entry in Other/Solution.xml | Evidence: E1 - the reviewer ran
    `pwsh provisioning/dataverse/ensure-schema.ps1 -Env dev` by hand (this session's own
    permission classifier refuses that live write), which reported CREATED for security role
    "REV Finance" and every privilege below (exit 0). The real id was then read back live via
    `roles?$filter=name eq 'REV Finance'&$select=roleid,name`: `13523850-a5af-f111-aaac-
    7ced8d43e1b4`, at the root business unit. Substituted below, exactly as A-TR-2 did for
    REV Trustee on 2026-08-21 and the 2026-08-14 fix did for REV Admin and REV Service
    Automation. The matching
    `<RootComponent type="20" id="{13523850-a5af-f111-aaac-7ced8d43e1b4}"/>` is added to
    Other/Solution.xml in the same change - both sides agree, per
    `scripts/verify-solution-root-components.py`. This id is correct for DEV only: TST/ACC
    and PRD get their own Dataverse-assigned ids when Pipelines promotes the role there for
    the first time (see the sibling roles' own notes on the same property) | Status: CLOSED.

  Before this fix, the id was a deliberate sentinel (`{ZZZZZZZZ-ZZZZ-ZZZZ-ZZZZ-
  ZZZZZZZZZZZZ}` - impossible GUID shape, Z falls outside a-f, chosen so a stale value would
  fail loudly at pack or import time rather than silently), the same convention Roles/REV
  Trustee/REV Trustee.xml's header used before that role's own id was closed - never a
  fabricated-but-plausible GUID, because roles are matched strictly by id on solution import
  and a plausible-looking wrong id would be invisible to review until the next import
  disagreed.
-->
<Role id="{13523850-a5af-f111-aaac-7ced8d43e1b4}" name="REV Finance">
  <IsInherited>2</IsInherited>
  <BusinessUnit>
    <IsRoot>1</IsRoot>
  </BusinessUnit>
  <IsCustomizable>1</IsCustomizable>
  <CanBeDeleted>1</CanBeDeleted>
  <IntroducedVersion>1.0.0.0</IntroducedVersion>
  <RolePrivileges>
      <!-- ===== Feature table privileges =====
           TAD section 6.2.1 deliverable #1: Create/Read/Write on rev_bankaccount and
           rev_payment (FR-150). rev_bankaccount and rev_payment are both UserOwned
           (Entities/rev_bankaccount/Entity.xml, Entities/rev_payment/Entity.xml), so Assign
           and Share both legitimately exist for them - deliberately NOT requested below: this
           role's only assignment path is the group-team binding above, and there is no
           product reason for a finance user to hand an individual Bank Account or Payment row
           to someone else. No Delete on either table: no requirement or FR in
           docs/plans/revitalise-payment-capture-plan.md asks for one, and a payment record
           existing at all is itself part of the audit trail this automation exists to create -
           removing one is not a documented use case, same reasoning REV Admin applies to
           rev_grant. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvCreaterev_bankaccount" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadrev_bankaccount" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvWriterev_bankaccount" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvAppendrev_bankaccount" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvAppendTorev_bankaccount" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvCreaterev_payment" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadrev_payment" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvWriterev_payment" level="Global" />
      <!-- TAD section 6.2.1 deliverable #2 (second half): Append on rev_payment, so a Payment
           row can be attached to its owning Bank Account / Provider / Grant lookups. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvAppendrev_payment" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvAppendTorev_payment" level="Global" />
      <!-- TAD section 6.2.1 deliverable #2 (first half), CORRECTION confirmed by the reviewer
           2026-09-09: Read + AppendTo on rev_grant. Section 6.2's originally-approved Finance
           row named no Grant privilege at all - a Payment cannot reference a Grant this role
           cannot read (FR-151), so this is what selecting a Grant on the payment capture
           surface (wbs:8.3) requires. READ-ONLY plus AppendTo: no Create/Write/Delete/Append -
           this role never authors or edits a Grant, it only attaches a Payment to one that
           already exists. See this file's header for the stated rev_amountawarded_base
           consequence of this grant. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadrev_grant" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvAppendTorev_grant" level="Global" />
      <!-- ===== rev_provider =====
           TAD section 6.2.1 deliverable #3, CORRECTION confirmed by the reviewer 2026-09-09:
           Create/Read/Write (section 6.2's originally-approved row said "read" only; FR-150
           requires this role to create and edit Providers on the payment capture surface).

           TAD section 6.2.1 deliverable #4 - NO prvAssignrev_provider AND NO
           prvSharerev_provider, AND THAT IS NOT A POLICY CHOICE - THOSE TWO PRIVILEGES DO NOT
           EXIST. rev_provider is OwnershipType=OrganizationOwned
           (Entities/rev_provider/Entity.xml): an organization-owned table has no individual
           owner, so there is nobody to assign a row TO and nobody to share it FROM, and
           Dataverse never creates an Assign or a Share privilege for it at all. Requesting
           one is not an over-grant the platform quietly ignores; it is a binding against a
           privilege GUID that cannot be resolved, and it FAILS - exactly the four-FAILED-line
           incident Roles/REV Admin/REV Admin.xml's own header records for 2026-08-24.
           `scripts/verify-role-privilege-ownership.py` derives the legal privilege set for
           every table from its own <OwnershipType> and enforces this generically; it is not
           re-run here from a hand-maintained table list, and it checks this role too, for
           free, the moment this file exists. No Delete: reference data this role reuses, not
           something the finance persona is documented to retire - no FR asks for it, unlike
           REV Admin's rev_provider block which does hold Delete for a different persona and a
           different reason (see that role's own comment). -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvCreaterev_provider" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadrev_provider" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvWriterev_provider" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvAppendrev_provider" level="Global" />
      <RolePrivilege name="prvAppendTorev_provider" level="Global" />
      <!-- ===== rev_anonymisedstatistic =====
           TAD section 6.2's summary row: "Anonymised Statistic: read." Read-only, Global, no
           Create/Write/Delete/Append/AppendTo - this role has no documented reason to author
           or edit an outcome snapshot, only to see it (parity with REV Trustee's own
           read-only grant on this table). rev_anonymisedstatistic is also
           OrganizationOwned (Entities/rev_anonymisedstatistic/Entity.xml), so - same reasoning
           as rev_provider above - no Assign, no Share: neither privilege exists for it. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadrev_anonymisedstatistic" level="Global" />
      <!-- ===== Platform baseline - see WARNING above (A-FIN-09) ===== -->
      <!-- Read own personal settings - required to open any model-driven app. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadUserSettings" level="Local" />
      <!-- Update own personal settings (time zone, language, default pane). -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvWriteUserSettings" level="Local" />
      <!-- Create the personal settings row on first sign-in. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvCreateUserSettings" level="Local" />
      <!-- Resolve user lookups rendered on screen (e.g. an application's owner column, where
           the payment capture surface shows Grant context). -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadUser" level="Local" />
      <!-- Resolve the owning business unit shown on every record. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadBusinessUnit" level="Local" />
      <!-- Read organisation-level settings such as date format and base currency. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadOrganization" level="Global" />
      <!-- Resolve the group team the role arrives through (C-TECH-040). -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadTeam" level="Local" />
      <!-- Resolve own role membership; required by the platform's own access checks. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadRole" level="Local" />
      <!-- Required by every money-typed column this role touches: rev_payment.rev_amount,
           and any money column surfaced from rev_grant (e.g. rev_amountawarded/
           rev_amountawarded_base). Without it those columns render blank, same reasoning as
           the two sibling roles. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadTransactionCurrency" level="Global" />
      <!-- Read own personal views. Kept for parity with the sibling MDA-persona roles; see
           A-FIN-09 above - not yet tested against the narrower alternative. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadUserQuery" level="Basic" />
      <!-- Create own personal views - the finance user's own working lists. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvCreateUserQuery" level="Basic" />
      <!-- Update own personal views. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvWriteUserQuery" level="Basic" />
      <!-- Delete own personal views. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvDeleteUserQuery" level="Basic" />
      <!-- Read the icons and resources a model-driven app loads. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadWebResource" level="Global" />
      <!-- Read the three environment variable definitions this solution ships. Kept for
           parity with the sibling roles; this role's own screens are not currently known to
           read one directly. -->
      <RolePrivilege name="prvReadEnvironmentVariableDefinition" level="Global" />
      <!-- ===== DELIBERATELY ABSENT - these omissions are controls, not gaps ===== -->
      <!-- No rev_applicant or rev_application privilege of any kind, of any level. TAD
           section 6.2's own row for this persona: "No Applicant or Application privilege."
           This is NFR-002's separation of duties from the other side - the finance role never
           reaches health/circumstance data, the same way REV Admin never reaches bank data
           (see that role's own header). -->
      <!-- No rev_review privilege of any kind - this persona has no trustee-review
           responsibility; nothing in TAD section 6.2 or docs/plans/revitalise-payment-
           capture-plan.md's FR-150-154 gives it one. -->
      <!-- No rev_setting privilege of any kind. Thresholds and configuration are an admin
           concern (TAD section 6.6); the finance role has no business reason to read or
           change them. -->
      <!-- No rev_errorlog privilege of any kind. Operational failures are an admin/service
           concern; nothing in this persona's requirements gives it visibility into the error
           log. -->
      <!-- No rev_roundfinance privilege of any kind. See this file's header - out of
           wbs:8.2's scope; REV Admin remains the interim maintainer (A-R25) until whoever
           owns that automation decides otherwise. -->
      <!-- No prvReadWorkflow - this persona never manages or views cloud flow run history;
           that is Admin/Service Automation territory (see REV Admin.xml). -->
      <!-- No audit-deletion privilege (prvDeleteAuditPartition or equivalent), and this role
           is never Dataverse System Administrator or Power Platform Administrator - same
           separation as the other three roles (TAD section 6.5, ADR-019, C-DOM-012). -->
  </RolePrivileges>
</Role>
